# SEO Workflow Rule

Use these project commands when running the SEO agent workflow.

## Custom Commands

- `/research <topic-or-url>`
  - Run Firecrawl scraping for external sources.
  - Save each raw scrape artifact under `/data/raw/`.
  - Include source URL, scrape timestamp, and crawl metadata.

- `/process <raw_file>`
  - Run `python agents/gemma_processor.py <raw_file>` (or the equivalent entrypoint that calls `clean_seo_data`).
  - Read from `/data/raw/` and write clean JSON reports to `/data/clean/`.
  - Preserve processing metadata (model, params, source file, timestamp).

## Hook Requirement

- A project hook must watch file edits for `/data/clean/`.
- When a clean file is created, append one line to `docs/workflow_state.md` with UTC timestamp and filename.
